{"name":"Riesling Grape","hex":"#bfb065","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"riesling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Riesling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riesling"},{"term":"grape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round, smooth-skinned edible fruit, usually purple, red, or green, that grows in bunches on female vines of most species of genus Vitis and the self-fertile plants of species Vitis vinifera.","Any woody vine of genus Vitis that bears clusters of grapes; a grapevine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing grapes or having a grape flavor.","Of a dark purplish red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Riesling","blocks":[{"text":"Riesling is a white grape variety that is believed to have originated from the Rhine Valley region of western Germany, before later being traced to the Alsace region by 1470 and Austria by 1700. Riesling is an aromatic grape variety displaying flowery, almost perfumed aromas as well as high acidity. It is used to make dry, semi-sweet, sweet, and sparkling white wines. Riesling wines are usually varietally pure and are seldom oaked. As of 2004, Riesling was estimated to be the world's 20th most grown variety at 48,700 hectares, but in terms of importance for quality wines, it is usually included in the \"top three\" white wine varieties together with Chardonnay and Sauvignon blanc. Riesling is a variety that is highly \"terroir-expressive\", meaning that the character of Riesling wines is greatly influenced by the wine's place of origin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Riesling_grapes_leaves.jpg/330px-Riesling_grapes_leaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riesling"},{"title":"Grape","blocks":[{"text":"A grape is a fruit, botanically a berry, of the deciduous woody vines of the flowering plant genus Vitis. Grapes are a non-climacteric type of fruit, generally occurring in clusters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grape"},{"title":"Shades of violet","blocks":[{"text":"Violet is a color term derived from the flower of the same name. There are numerous variations of the color violet, a sampling of which are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Color_icon_violet_v3.svg/330px-Color_icon_violet_v3.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_violet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Kabinet_Riesling_from_Graacher_Himmelreich.jpg/500px-Kabinet_Riesling_from_Graacher_Himmelreich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Kabinet_Riesling_from_Graacher_Himmelreich.jpg/1280px-Kabinet_Riesling_from_Graacher_Himmelreich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Kabinet_Riesling_from_Graacher_Himmelreich.jpg/500px-Kabinet_Riesling_from_Graacher_Himmelreich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Kabinett-level German Riesling from the Mosel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKabinet_Riesling_from_Graacher_Himmelreich.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Riesling_Kabinett_1975_in_glass.jpg/500px-Riesling_Kabinett_1975_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0